[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Core Types, Integrity, QoS, Concepts, and State Machines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Strongly Typed Core Domain and Value-Error Primitives
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware core shall provide strongly typed TaiTimestamp, DurationNs (with compile-time _ns, _us, _ms, and _s literals), GenId, Status, CmdStage, CmdResult, and a zero-exception, zero-heap [[nodiscard]] Expected<T, E> template (including void specialization).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Strong types eliminate raw integer unit confusion while Expected<T, E> enforces explicit error handling without C++ exception overhead.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/core/expected.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Compile-Time and Runtime Castagnoli CRC-32C Engine
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a constexpr and runtime Castagnoli CRC-32C implementation (reflected polynomial 0x82F63B78) verified at compile time against the standard check vector (0xE3069283 for ASCII 123456789).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single verified CRC-32C primitive provides fast, consistent data integrity verification across parameter banks, persistent checkpoints, data descriptors, and memory scrubbing.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/core/crc32c.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Compile-Time Static Quality-of-Service Contracts
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall allow every Blackboard, SpscChannel, and DataTopic to bind a compile-time QoSConfig specifying Durability (Volatile or TransientLocal), Reliability (Guaranteed or BestEffortDropOldest), Deadline, Liveliness, LeaseTimeout, and History depth with zero runtime discovery overhead.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Static compile-time QoS enforces explicit staleness, back-pressure, and crash-reclamation semantics without dynamic broker or discovery complexity.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/core/qos.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: C++20 Concepts and Zero-Vtable Component Wiring
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall enforce component, wire-POD, power-of-two ring capacity, doorbell, clock, and MMIO register transport contracts via C++20 concepts with static compile-time dispatch and zero generated inheritance base classes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Pure C++20 concepts deliver strong interface checking and optimal inlined bare-metal codegen without external DSL lock-in or virtual dispatch overhead.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/core/concepts.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Zero-Allocation Table-Driven Finite State Machine
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a deterministic, zero-allocation Fsm template supporting declarative transition tables, guard predicates, transition actions, transition counters, and explicit GuardRejected and UnhandledEvent status reporting.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Mode management, self-test sequences, and hardware lifecycle state machines require auditable, deterministic transition logic without dynamic memory or virtual state objects.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/core/fsm.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Inter-Partition Communication and Persistent State Primitives

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Lock-Free Seqlock Blackboard Primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a cache-line-aligned Seqlock Blackboard (BlackboardStorage, BlackboardWriter, BlackboardReader) supporting non-blocking single-writer publishing, bounded-retry lock-free reading, Volatile vs. TransientLocal durability, and explicit DeadlineMissed staleness detection.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Pull-sampled shared-memory blackboards decouple housekeeping and shared state producers from telemetry collectors, eliminating queue overflows and priority inversion during anomalies.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/blackboard.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-007
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Cache-Line-Isolated Lock-Free SPSC Channel
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a cache-line-isolated Single-Producer Single-Consumer ring (128-byte SpscHeader separating producer head and consumer tail onto distinct 64-byte cache lines) supporting power-of-two depth, peer GenId validation, interrupt-coalesced doorbell wakeups, and bounded WCET drain_up_to processing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Separating producer and consumer cache lines eliminates false sharing across cores while generation validation and bounded draining guarantee deterministic control-plane IPC.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/spsc_channel.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-008
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Bounded Rate-Capped and Deduplicating Event Ring
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a per-partition bounded EventWriter supporting runtime severity-bitmask filtering, fixed-size binary EventRecord emission, per-event-ID cooldown suppression with repeat_count aggregation, and unconditional Fatal-event bypass of filtering and cooldowns.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Local burst deduplication prevents a noisy payload anomaly from flooding downlink event buffers or masking critical flight-system alerts.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/event_ring.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-009
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Double-Buffered CRC-32C Parameter Bank
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a double-buffered ParamBank supporting range/invariant validation during shadow-bank staging, CRC-32C integrity protection, atomic minor-frame commit, atomic rollback to the prior valid bank, and runtime verify_active SEU checking.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Atomic bank flipping eliminates torn multi-parameter configuration updates and allows safe on-orbit calibration changes with instant rollback.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/param_bank.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-010
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Ping-Pong Crash-Atomic CriticalStore
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a ping-pong double-buffered CriticalStore stamped with magic, monotonic sequence number, 64-bit MANIFEST_HASH, and CRC-32C such that an upset or crash during a checkpoint write automatically falls back to the prior intact verified slot upon WarmStart restore.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Crash-atomic warm-reset persistence enables sub-2 ms recovery of instrument modes, calibration epochs, and counters across SEU restarts and spare-slot failovers without flash wear.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/critical_store.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Zero-Copy Data Plane, Hardware Slot Contract, and Runtime

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-011
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Atomic Bitmask FramePool and Linear Move-Only FrameLease
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a static XMPU-aligned FramePool tracking exclusive producer and concurrent Read-Only subscriber ownership via an idempotent atomic bitmask per slot, wrapped by non-copyable [[nodiscard]] FrameLease and ReadOnlyFrameView RAII handles that automatically release slots on scope exit.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Move-only linear handles prevent buffer leaks at compile time while atomic bitmask ownership makes double-free races mathematically impossible even under concurrent FDIR reclamation.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/data/frame_lease.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-012
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Zero-Copy One-to-Many DataTopic with Crash Lease Reclamation
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a 1-to-N DataTopic publishing only 32-byte FrameDesc metadata to subscriber descriptor rings while payload bytes remain stationary in memory, enforcing Guaranteed (lossless) vs. BestEffortDropOldest (non-blocking shed) per subscriber and supporting timeout-based lease reclamation and crashed-subscriber revocation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Direct 1-to-N zero-copy fan-out allows recorders, quick-look downlinks, and onboard analytics to share multi-Gbps sensor frames simultaneously without splitter components or CPU copies, while preventing stalled payloads from starving critical recorders.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/data/data_topic.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-013
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Compile-Time Access-Enforced MMIO RegMap
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide compile-time typed MMIO register definitions enforcing RO, WO, RW, and RW1C (write-1-to-clear) access policies over any RegisterTransport backend (direct volatile AXI4-Lite MMIO, host MockRegisterBank, or Verilator RTL bridge).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Compile-time access enforcement eliminates invalid register reads/writes at build time while decoupling drivers from physical memory addresses for host SIL and RTL testing.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/hw/reg_map.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-014
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Unified Hardware SlotHandle and 4 KB SCSR Contract
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a unified SlotHandle operating over the standardized 4 KB Slot Control and Status Register (SCSR) layout to verify magic and 64-bit MANIFEST_HASH, inspect SlotState, issue uniform SlotCmd transitions, clear RW1C faults, kick the hardware slot watchdog, and read hardware-latched 64-bit TAI timestamps across static spatial PL, dynamic DFX PL, and AIE slots.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One uniform hardware-software slot contract allows static spatial and dynamically reconfigurable instruments to share identical lifecycle, watchdog, and FDIR management software.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/hw/slot_handle.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-015
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Zero-Thread CyclicScheduler and Unique-Opcode CommandRouter
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide a compile-time unrolled CyclicScheduler supporting periodic rate groups and phased tick windows without per-component RTOS threads, paired with a zero-vtable CommandRouter that rejects duplicate command opcodes at compile time via static_assert.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Eliminating per-component threads and dynamic registration tables lowers RAM usage, improves cache locality, and prevents runtime opcode collisions.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/runtime/partition_runtime.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-MW-016
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Composable Per-Partition Subtopology Bundles
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware shall provide parameterized C++20 template Subtopology bundles (such as CdhBundle, CommsBundle, StorageBundle, and FdirBundle) allowing distinct partitions within the same mission build to instantiate independent queue depths, pool sizes, and safety profiles without global configuration collisions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Per-partition template parameterization eliminates monolithic single-config build bottlenecks while preserving rapid mission assembly.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/runtime/subtopology.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-001

[[/SECTION]]
